The JMAP sent-observation test moves this message into the account's Sent
collection and back, to prove that a message which *enters* Sent through a state
change still yields its recipients.

It owns a unique recipient address, addressed nowhere else in the seed, so the
assertion cannot be satisfied by another fixture and two live suites running
concurrently cannot see each other's observation.

APPENDed into its own mailbox for the same reason as 08-jmap-state.eml: a JMAP
move replaces an Email's mailboxIds, so moving a COPY would drag the shared
baseline out of the count-asserted mailboxes.
